<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      THE ONLY PLACE IN THE TREE WHERE THIS IS FALSE.

      Dropping FLAG_SECURE lets `adb exec-out screencap` return a real image instead of a black
      frame, which is what makes UI work verifiable at all — a uiautomator dump describes the node
      tree and can say nothing about a gradient, a halo or the smoothness of a ring.

      This is the `debug` build-type source set. Release variants do not compile it, so a shipped
      APK has no path to this value; `checkScreenSecurity` asserts that on the merged release
      resources of both flavours on every push.

      Two consequences of dropping the flag in debug, stated so they are decisions and not
      discoveries: the app-switcher preview is no longer obscured either (recents blocking is a
      side effect of FLAG_SECURE itself — there is no separate onPause blur), and screen recording
      is possible. Both are wanted in a QA build and neither reaches users.

      In effect since 2026-08-10.
    -->
    <bool name="lk_obscure_screen">false</bool>
</resources>
